# openssl: a fix exists in Debian's own package repo (3.5.7-1~deb13u3) but
# the python:3.12-slim base image had not yet been rebuilt against it as
# of the digest pinned in the Dockerfile - checked directly against Docker
# Hub's tags API before writing this, not assumed. DoS via QUIC flow
# control / DTLS retransmission info disclosure - this container makes no
# QUIC or DTLS connections of any kind.
CVE-2026-75804
CVE-2026-84782

# --- cosign v3.1.3's own compiled-in Go dependencies. cosign is used here
# for exactly one thing: `cosign verify-blob` against a local file and a
# local signature bundle, as a subprocess - no gRPC server, no HTML/XML
# template rendering, no long-lived network listener. v3.1.3 is confirmed
# the current latest cosign release (checked against the live GitHub
# releases API); every fix below exists in a newer Go module version, not
# yet in a cosign release that pulls it in. Most of these CVEs are in
# server-side or parsing code paths a client-side `verify-blob` call never
# reaches (grpc-go's own server DoS, html/template XSS, encoding/xml
# recursion, net/http server-side HTTP/2 issues) - listed anyway, since
# cosign compiles the whole dependency in regardless of which code path
# this project's own usage exercises.
CVE-2026-33818
CVE-2026-39821
CVE-2026-39822
CVE-2026-46600
CVE-2026-56852
CVE-2026-56853
